{"id":"plo_tzlich","lemma":"plötzlich","pos":"adv","rank":611,"glosses":["suddenly, abruptly"],"ipa":"/ˈplœt͡slɪç/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/6e/De-pl%C3%B6tzlich.ogg/De-pl%C3%B6tzlich.ogg.mp3","examples":[{"text":"Warum ist es plötzlich so still?","en":"Why is it so quiet all of a sudden?","words":[{"g":"why"},{"g":"is","l":"sein"},{"g":"it"},null,{"g":"so"},{"g":"quiet, silent"}]},{"text":"Plötzlich ging das Licht an.","en":"The light came on suddenly.","words":[null,{"g":"to go, to walk","l":"gehen"},{"g":"the / that"},{"g":"light"},{"g":"at / on"}]},{"text":"Mir kam plötzlich eine gute Idee.","en":"Suddenly, a good idea occurred to me.","words":[{"g":"(to) me","l":"ich"},{"g":"to come","l":"kommen"},null,{"g":"a"},{"g":"good","l":"gut"},{"g":"idea"}]},{"text":"Er wurde plötzlich krank.","en":"He suddenly fell ill.","words":[{"g":"he / it"},{"g":"to become","l":"werden"},null,{"g":"ill, sick"}]},{"text":"Das Ende kam plötzlich.","en":"The end came suddenly.","words":[{"g":"the / that"},{"g":"end, finish"},{"g":"to come","l":"kommen"},null]}]}